    "darkAdapted": false,
    "isDigitalEntity": false,
    "notes": "<p><i>A tiny, translucent, gelatinous parasite, lacking intelligence, latches onto a host's spinal or adrenal regions.</i></p><p><strong>Movement:</strong> CLOSE (climb)</p>",
    "description": "<p><strong>Attacks:</strong> 1 Tendril Latch +1 (1d4 + attach)</p><p><strong>Attach.</strong> Attach to target. DC to remove is equal to 9 + its current HP.</p><p>Adrenal</p><p><strong>Leech.</strong> When attached to a host, the Adrenoid increases the host's STR and DEX by +2 but compels uncontrollable aggression. The host must succeed on a WIS check (DC 12) each round to avoid attacking the nearest living creature.</p><p>Sympathetic</p><p><strong>Surge.</strong> The Adrenoid gains 1 HP every time the host deals melee damage.</p>",
